// FDRA popup expression in "CA Fire Weather Intelligence Map" (item 0b083c059dc8442ca7c9e6a8842e3ca1).
// Live roll-up of the FDRA's FDOP stations (field station_ids, from the 2026 Forest Thresholds sheet)
// against each forest's custom thresholds. Values that are thresholds (not FDRA ids) are NOT committed
// here on purpose — they live in the web map; see the threshold table in the build notes.
//
// Logic:
//   1. live = CA NFDRS 3.0 RAWS whose stationId is in station_ids (fallback: RAWS inside the FDRA)
//   2. average ERC / BI and their percentiles
//   3. class by forest rule:
//        BDF   BI staffing (5 class) + dispatch (4 class) breakpoints per FDRA
//        ENF   335 BI dispatch + ERC staffing, peak (May 1–Nov 15) / non-peak breakpoints
//        SRF   BI vs forest 90th / 97th values per FDRA
//        TNF   BI vs custom pair (index to confirm)
//        SQF   custom pair shown, index pending
//        other ERC / BI vs 90th / 97th using the live percentile
//   4. FDRAs with fuel model X or Z show a warning: the live layer is fuel model Y only.
